@prefix mpc:     <https://sparq.dev/ns/mpc#> .
@prefix secx:    <https://w3id.org/zkp-sparql/sec-prop#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

# secprop-illustrative-control.ttl — TEST-ONLY positive control for
# tests/secprop_admissibility.rs. NOT part of the shipped annotation graph
# (`sparq_mpc::secprop::annotations_n3()` carries only implemented protocols).
#
# sparq-mpc implements NO malicious-secure, dishonest-majority protocol: the SPDZ
# regime is explicitly NOT entered (design route (b), bead sq-j5ok), and
# `BackendRegistry::select(&SecurityRequirement::dishonest_majority_malicious())`
# fail-closed REFUSES rather than downgrading. This block exists so the ORDER on
# both dimensions has a positive control — a subject a strict preference ADMITS —
# so the exclusion tests cannot pass vacuously. It is a sparq-local illustrative
# IRI, named so it is unmistakably not a shipped capability; the same device as
# `zk:illustrative-source-bbs-2023` in the sparq-zk annotation graph.

mpc:illustrative-spdz-dishonest-majority
  rdfs:comment "ILLUSTRATIVE ONLY — sparq-mpc does NOT implement this. A hypothetical SPDZ-style malicious, dishonest-majority protocol, present so the secx:AdversaryModel / secx:CorruptionThreshold orders have a positive control in the admissibility tests. Selecting a dishonest-majority-malicious backend from sparq-mpc's registry is refused (MpcError::NoBackendSatisfies); the regime is deferred (bead sq-j5ok)."@en-GB ;
  secx:hasProperty
    [ secx:property secx:AdversaryModel ; secx:level secx:Malicious ;
      secx:assurance secx:Conjectured ] ,
    [ secx:property secx:CorruptionThreshold ; secx:level secx:DishonestMajority ;
      secx:assurance secx:Conjectured ] .
